#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:4
msgid "Lyapunov exponent computation"
msgstr "Cálculo de expoentes de Lyapunov"

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:7
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr "Motivação"

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:9
msgid ""
"In chaotic dynamics, the **largest Lyapunov exponent** :math:`\\lambda_{\\max}` "
"quantifies how quickly two initially nearby trajectories diverge from each "
"other.  If :math:`\\lambda_{\\max} > 0`, the system is chaotic — a tiny "
"perturbation in the initial condition grows exponentially and the long-term "
"behaviour becomes unpredictable.  If :math:`\\lambda_{\\max} \\le 0`, the "
"system is periodic or stable."
msgstr "In chaotic dynamics, the **largest Lyapunov exponent** :math:`\\lambda_{\\max}` quantifies how quickly two initially nearby trajectories diverge from each other.  If :math:`\\lambda_{\\max} > 0`, the system is chaotic — a tiny perturbation in the initial condition grows exponentially and the long-term behaviour becomes unpredictable.  If :math:`\\lambda_{\\max} \\le 0`, the system is periodic or stable."

#: ../../source/algorithms/lyapunov.rst:17
msgid ""
"For chaotic communication, :math:`\\lambda_{\\max}` is the single most "
"important diagnostic: it tells us whether the Hénon map with a given "
"FIR filter still preserves chaos, or whether the filter *killed* the "
"chaos (making the scheme useless for physical-layer security)."
msgstr ""
"Para comunicação caótica, :math:`\\lambda_{\\max}` é o diagnóstico mais "
"importante: ele indica se o mapa de Hénon com um dado filtro FIR ainda "
"preserva o caos, ou se o filtro *matou* o caos (tornando o esquema inútil "
"para segurança de camada física)."

